{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/128618-immortal-the-gathering-20th-anniversary-edition","id":128618,"title":"Immortal: the Gathering 20th Anniversary Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-08T16:42:52-07:00","id":128618,"title":"Immortal: the Gathering 20th Anniversary Edition","content":"So way back in the 90's some guys wrote a splat book for one of the best settings ever made so that they could be played in OWoD. It was updated for 10 years until the end of OWoD. Later was remade for NWoD. With the emergence of the 20th Anniversary books, I thought it would be fun to bring back the old splat book with updated rules. Here's the first copy of the book and character sheet (thanks for the help Mr. Gone).<br /> <br /> I don't think there's a setting other than Vampire the Masquerade to describe the 90's other than Highlander. It fits so well into the Old World of Darkness that it makes you mess your leg warmers and guys having crazy long hair. For those of you who've never seen Highlander I recommend actually taking some time out of your busy schedule and do a viewing of the first movie on Netflix. Don't watch the other movies. Just the TV show and the first movie.<br /> <br /> Now you can all blast Queen while dueling each other with your crazy lightning infused Katanas. Enjoy. (Queen music, katanas, and long hair not included).<br /> <br /> Remember guys, don't lose your head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://a.pomf.se/tsstou.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://a.pomf.se/tsstou.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://a.pomf.se/tsstou.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://a.pomf.se/tsstou.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T18:32:45-07:00","id":128676,"title":"","content":"Cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though I have a rule question. Speed of the Stag allows for extra actions during one turn, but it says that fatigues an immortal as the Empower Self ability. Empower Self leaves an immortal fatigued for hours. Does this mean that simply using Speed of the Stag for 1 turn will leave the Immortal fatigued for an hour? Also, does using Quickening powers take an action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T19:42:56-07:00","id":128700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/128618-immortal-the-gathering-20th-anniversary-edition?p=128676#post128676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though I have a rule question. Speed of the Stag allows for extra actions during one turn, but it says that fatigues an immortal as the Empower Self ability. Empower Self leaves an immortal fatigued for hours. Does this mean that simply using Speed of the Stag for 1 turn will leave the Immortal fatigued for an hour? Also, does using Quickening powers take an action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good questions.<br /> <br /> First one, it's suppose to follow it on a per roll basis, I'll be sure to fix that, however you can pop it at any time and the fatigue will go away until it ends. Speed of the Stag is suppose to be a short term power made for duels and combat mostly. It also is suppose to work with not just Stags but other animals giving a variety of effects, like extra soak, dexterity, and strength based on the animal you last synced with. Stag is just the go to one for most because Celerity.<br /> <br /> Second one, yes and no. It will state which ones use a turn and which ones won't. Unless it's stated to take a turn, it's considered not to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}